                                "sense_id": "1a248084-c709-313b-99d7-71e03dacd2c7",
                                "text": "Gradually the hedges and fields give way before long rows of houses; and a few single domiciles, with plats of turf cut into patterns, and bunches of daisies dusty and dry as if just dropped from the wreath of a figurante, are what the orientals call so pleasant and rural, so convenient for stages and Sunday."
